tabetic.en:
a. Of or pertaining to tabes; of the nature of tabes;
   affected with tabes; tabid.
n. One affected with tabes.

tache.en:
n. Something used for taking hold or holding; a catch; a loop;
   a button.
n. A spot, stain, or blemish.

talismanical.en:
a. Of or pertaining to a talisman; having the properties
   of a talisman, or preservative against evils by occult influence;
   magical.

tallowing.en:
p. pr. & vb. n. of Tallow
n. The act, or art, of causing animals to produce tallow;
   also, the property in animals of producing tallow.

tared.en:
imp. & p. p. of Tare
a. Weighed; determined; reduced to equal or standard weight;
   as, tared filter papers, used in weighing precipitates.

tempean.en:
a. Of or pertaining to Temple, a valley in Thessaly,
   celebrated by Greek poets on account of its beautiful scenery;
   resembling Temple; hence, beautiful; delightful; charming.

termless.en:
a. Having no term or end; unlimited; boundless; unending;
   as, termless time.
a. Inexpressible; indescribable.

testudinarious.en:
a. Of or pertaining to the shell of a tortoise;
   resembling a tortoise shell; having the color or markings of a tortoise
   shell.

tetrachord.en:
n. A scale series of four sounds, of which the extremes,
   or first and last, constituted a fourth. These extremes were immutable;
   the two middle sounds were changeable.

thew.en:
n. Manner; custom; habit; form of behavior; qualities of mind;
   disposition; specifically, good qualities; virtues.
n. Muscle or strength; nerve; brawn; sinew.

throats.en:
n. the passage to the stomach and lungs; in the front part of the neck below the chin and above the collarbone
n. an opening in the vamp of a shoe at the instep
n. a passage resembling a throat in shape or function;

tibiotarsal.en:
a. Of or pertaining to both to the tibia and the tarsus;
   as, the tibiotarsal articulation.
a. Of or pertaining to the tibiotarsus.

triparted.en:
a. Parted into three piece; having three parts or pieces;
   -- said of the field or of a bearing; as, a cross triparted.
a. Divided nearly to the base into three segments or lobes.

tripolitan.en:
a. Of or pertaining to Tripoli or its inhabitants;
   Tripoline.
n. A native or inhabitant of Tripoli.

trisnitrate.en:
n. A nitrate formed from three molecules of nitric acid;
   also, less properly, applied to certain basic nitrates; as, trisnitrate
   of bismuth.

triturate.en:
v. t. To rub, grind, bruise, or thrash.
v. t. To rub or grind to a very fine or impalpable powder;
   to pulverize and comminute thoroughly.

triumphing.en:
p. pr. & vb. n. of Triumph
a. Having or celebrating a triumph; victorious;
   triumphant.

tryptics.en:
plural of tryptic
a. Relating to trypsin or to its action; produced by trypsin;
   as, trypsin digestion.

tumultuary.en:
a. Attended by, or producing, a tumult; disorderly;
   promiscuous; confused; tumultuous.
a. Restless; agitated; unquiet.

turgent.en:
a. Rising into a tumor, or a puffy state; swelling; tumid;
   as, turgent humors.
a. Inflated; bombastic; turgid; pompous.
